-- wra1-sch2.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), Schedule 2 (universal credit: amendments), part wra1.
-- LAYER 1, the law objectively: it takes nobody's point of view.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script, not the official text.
--
-- Schedule 2 amends other Acts, which are not among the sources. Short names for the host Acts (PLAN.md section 6):
-- SSAA Social Security Administration Act 1992; JSA Jobseekers Act 1995; SSA1998 Social Security Act 1998; SSFA Social Security
-- Fraud Act 2001; SPCA State Pension Credit Act 2002; CSA1991 Child Support Act 1991; WRA2007 Welfare Reform Act 2007.
-- Initials used once here for the others: CA1989 Children Act 1989; LGFA Local Government Finance Act 1992; EA1996 Education Act
-- 1996; SSRBA1997 Social Security (Recovery of Benefits) Act 1997; IAA1999 Immigration and Asylum Act 1999; CSPSSA2000 Child
-- Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000.
-- The raw text prints no paragraph numbers and Schedule 2 has one cross-heading per host Act, not one per paragraph, so no
-- paragraph number is derived: a label is "sch 2", the host Act's short name, and the host provision as the text names it.
--
-- What an amendment that adds universal credit to a list of the host provision means for the individual is what the host
-- provision says about that list, and that is not among the sources. So the list functions answer one thing: whether the
-- amendment puts universal credit (or the thing it names) in the host provision. They never claim a consequence.
-- An amendment that is housekeeping (a conjunction repealed, a cross-reference changed, an Act added to a list of Acts used by
-- officials) is machinery and has a row in the coverage table, not a function.
-- Reading an answer (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed and not ruled by a lawyer):
--   FALSE / JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (quoted in a FALSE-kind comment), or a supplied regulation says no
--   NOTHING            = not covered (the reason is in a NOTHING-kind comment)

§ `Schedule 2 -- the host provisions that now include universal credit`

-- Every amending paragraph in the Schedule that adds universal credit (or receipt or entitlement) to the host provision's list.
