-- src:2729 | After section 159C there is inserted—
-- src:2730 | 159D Effect of alterations affecting universal credit
-- src:2731 | (1) Subject to such exceptions and conditions as may be prescribed, subsection (2) or (3) shall have effect where—
-- src:2732 | (a) an award of universal credit is in force in favour of any person (“the recipient”), and
-- src:2733 | (b) an alteration—
-- src:2734 | (i) in any element of universal credit,
-- src:2735 | (ii) in the recipient's benefit income,
-- src:2736 | (iii) in any amount to be deducted in respect of earned income under section 8(3)(a) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012,
-- src:2737 | (iv) in any component of a contribution-based jobseeker's allowance,
-- src:2738 | (v) in any component of a contributory employment and support allowance, or
-- src:2739 | (vi) in such other matters as may be prescribed,
-- src:2740 | affects the computation of the amount of universal credit to which he is entitled.
-- src:2741 | (2) Where, as a result of the alteration, the amount of universal credit to which the recipient is entitled is increased or reduced, then, as from the commencing date, the amount of universal credit payable in the case of the recipient under the award shall be the increased or reduced amount, without any further decision of the Secretary of State; and the award shall have effect accordingly.
-- src:2742 | (3) Where, notwithstanding the alteration, the recipient continues on and after the commencing date to be entitled to the same amount by way of universal credit as before, the award shall continue in force accordingly.
-- src:2743 | (4) Subsection (5) applies where a statement is made in the House of Commons by or on behalf of the Secretary of State which specifies—
-- src:2744 | (a) in relation to any of the items referred to in subsection (1)(b)(i) to (vi), the amount of the alteration which he proposes to make by an order under section 150, 150A or 152 or by or under any other enactment, and
-- src:2745 | (b) the date on which he proposes to bring the alteration in force (“the proposed commencing date”).
-- src:2746 | (5) If, in a case where this subsection applies, an award of universal credit is made in favour of a person before the proposed commencing date and after the date on which the statement is made, the award—
-- src:2747 | (a) may provide for the universal credit to be paid as from the proposed commencing date at a rate determined by reference to the amounts of the items referred to in subsection (1)(b)(i) to (vi) which will be in force on that date, or
-- src:2748 | (b) may be expressed in terms of the amounts of those items in force at the date of the award.
-- src:2749 | (6) In this section—
-- src:2750 | “alteration”—
-- src:2751 | in relation to any element of universal credit, means its alteration by or under any enactment;
-- src:2752 | in relation to a person's benefit income, means the alteration of any of the sums referred to in section 150 or 150A by any enactment or by an order under section 150, 150A or 152 to the extent that any such alteration affects the amount of his benefit income;
-- src:2753 | in relation to any component of a contribution-based jobseeker's allowance or a contributory employment and support allowance, means its alteration by or under any enactment;
-- src:2754 | in relation to any other matter, has such meaning as may be prescribed;
-- src:2755 | “benefit income”, in relation to a person, means so much of his income as consists of benefit under the Contributions and Benefits Act or personal independence payment;
-- src:2756 | “the commencing date”, in relation to an alteration, means the date on which the alteration comes into force in relation to the recipient;
-- src:2757 | “component”—
-- src:2758 | in relation to contribution-based jobseeker's allowance, means any of the sums specified in regulations under the Jobseekers Act 1995 which are relevant in calculating the amount payable by way of a jobseeker's allowance;
-- src:2759 | in relation to a contributory employment and support allowance, means any of the sums specified in regulations under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 which are relevant in calculating the amount payable by way of such an allowance;
-- src:2760 | “element”, in relation to universal credit, means any of the amounts specified in regulations under sections 9 to 12 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 which are included in the calculation of an award of universal credit.
-- src:2761 | After section 160B there is inserted—
-- src:2762 | 160C Implementation of increases in universal credit due to attainment of a particular age
-- src:2763 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:2764 | (a) an award of universal credit is in force in favour of a person (“the recipient”), and
-- src:2765 | (b) an element has become applicable, or applicable at a particular rate, because he or some other person has reached a particular age (“the qualifying age”).
-- src:2766 | (2) If, as a result of the recipient or other person reaching the qualifying age, the recipient becomes entitled to an increased amount of universal credit, the amount payable to or for him under the award shall, as from the day on which he becomes so entitled, be that increased amount, without any further decision of the Secretary of State; and the award shall have effect accordingly.
-- src:2767 | (3) Subsection (2) does not apply where, in consequence of the recipient or other person reaching the qualifying age, a question arises in relation to the recipient's entitlement to—
-- src:2768 | (a) a benefit under the Contribution and Benefits Act, or
-- src:2769 | (b) personal independence payment.
-- src:2770 | (4) Subsection (2) does not apply where, in consequence of the recipient or other person reaching the qualifying age, a question arises in relation to the recipient's entitlement to universal credit, other than—
-- src:2771 | (a) the question whether the element concerned, or any other element, becomes or ceases to be applicable, or applicable at a particular rate, in the recipient's case, and
-- src:2772 | (b) the question whether, in consequence, the amount of his universal credit falls to be varied.
-- src:2773 | (5) In this section, “element”, in relation to universal credit, means any of the amounts specified in regulations under sections 9 to 12 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 which are included in the calculation of an award of universal credit.
