@ref sch 2 (src:2681-2922)
GIVEN provision IS A `sch 2 host provision`
      `the circumstances regulations prescribe apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 the host provision now includes universal credit` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    -- Children Act 1989: "of universal credit (except in such circumstances as may be prescribed)"
    WHEN `sch 2 CA1989 s 17(9)` THEN `universal credit, except in the circumstances prescribed`
    WHEN `sch 2 CA1989 s 17A(5)(b)` THEN `universal credit, except in the circumstances prescribed`
    WHEN `sch 2 CA1989 s 29(3) and (3A)` THEN `universal credit, except in the circumstances prescribed`
    WHEN `sch 2 CA1989 Sch 2 para 21(4)` THEN `universal credit, except in the circumstances prescribed`
    -- Child Support Act 1991, and Education Act 1996: universal credit "in such circumstances as may be prescribed"
    WHEN `sch 2 CSA1991 Sch 1 para 5(4)` THEN `universal credit, only in the circumstances prescribed`
    WHEN `sch 2 EA1996 s 457(4)(b)` THEN `universal credit, only in the circumstances prescribed`
    WHEN `sch 2 EA1996 s 512ZB(4)(a)` THEN `universal credit, only in the circumstances prescribed`
    WHEN `sch 2 EA1996 s 512ZB(4)(b)` THEN `universal credit, only in the circumstances prescribed`
    -- the other amending paragraphs add universal credit with no condition of their own
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 1(4)(za)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 5(2)(za)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 5(6)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 74(2)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 74A(7)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 78(6)(d)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 105(1)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 106(1) to (4)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 108(1)(a)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 109(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 126(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 130(1)(za)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 132(1)(za)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 150(1)(n)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 187(1)(za)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA s 191 definition of benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 LGFA Sch 4 para 6(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 LGFA Sch 4 para 6(2)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 LGFA Sch 4 para 12(1)(aa)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 LGFA Sch 4 para 12(1)(d)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 LGFA Sch 8 para 6(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 LGFA Sch 8 para 6(2)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 JSA s 2(3C) definition of benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSRBA1997 s 29 definition of benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSRBA1997 Sch 2 table` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSA1998 s 8(3)(aa)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSA1998 s 27(7)(f)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 IAA1999 s 97(5)(za)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 IAA1999 s 115(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 CSPSSA2000 s 69(1)(a)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSFA s 9(1)(za)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSFA s 10(3)(bd)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 WRA2007 Sch 1 para 1(5)(za)` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a host provision the Schedule does not amend is not covered
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `universal credit, except in the circumstances prescribed` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the circumstances regulations prescribe apply`
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(except in such circumstances as may be prescribed)": in those circumstances universal credit is not included
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the circumstances are prescribed, and regulations are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        `universal credit, only in the circumstances prescribed` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the circumstances regulations prescribe apply`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "universal credit (in such circumstances as may be prescribed)": outside those circumstances universal credit is not included
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the circumstances are prescribed, and regulations are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `Schedule 2 -- Social Security Administration Act 1992, sections 159D and 160C`

-- 159D(6) "'benefit income', in relation to a person, means so much of his income as consists of benefit under the Contributions
-- and Benefits Act or personal independence payment".
DECLARE `sch 2 SSAA 159D(6) kind of income` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 SSAA 159D(6) benefit under the Contributions and Benefits Act`
    `sch 2 SSAA 159D(6) personal independence payment`
    `sch 2 SSAA 159D(6) some other income`

-- src:2755 | “benefit income”, in relation to a person, means so much of his income as consists of benefit under the Contributions and Benefits Act or personal independence payment;
@ref sch 2 SSAA 159D(6) (src:2755-2755)
GIVEN kind IS A `sch 2 SSAA 159D(6) kind of income`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 2 SSAA 159D(6) the income is benefit income` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA 159D(6) benefit under the Contributions and Benefits Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 SSAA 159D(6) personal independence payment` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'benefit income' ... means so much of his income as consists of benefit under the Contributions and Benefits Act or personal independence payment"
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 159D(6) "'element', in relation to universal credit, means any of the amounts specified in regulations under sections 9 to
-- 12 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 which are included in the calculation of an award of universal credit." The same words are
-- in 160C(5).
-- src:2760 | “element”, in relation to universal credit, means any of the amounts specified in regulations under sections 9 to 12 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 which are included in the calculation of an award of universal credit.
@ref sch 2 SSAA 159D(6) (src:2760-2760)
GIVEN `the amount is specified in regulations under sections 9 to 12` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount is included in the calculation of an award of universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 SSAA 159D(6) the amount is an element of universal credit` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'element' ... means any of the amounts specified in regulations under sections 9 to 12 ... which are included in the calculation of an award" (a definition); NOTHING where the regulations are not supplied
    `s 3(1) both of these are true` `the amount is specified in regulations under sections 9 to 12` (JUST `the amount is included in the calculation of an award of universal credit`)

-- 159D(1) "Subject to such exceptions and conditions as may be prescribed, subsection (2) or (3) shall have effect where (a) an
-- award of universal credit is in force in favour of any person ('the recipient'), and (b) an alteration ... affects the
-- computation of the amount of universal credit to which he is entitled."
-- 159D(2) "Where, as a result of the alteration, the amount of universal credit to which the recipient is entitled is increased
-- or reduced, then, as from the commencing date, the amount of universal credit payable in the case of the recipient under the
-- award shall be the increased or reduced amount, without any further decision of the Secretary of State; and the award shall
-- have effect accordingly." Subsection (3) says the same of an award whose amount does not change, so one function answers
-- for both: the amount payable from the commencing date is the amount to which the recipient is entitled after the alteration.
-- src:2731 | (1) Subject to such exceptions and conditions as may be prescribed, subsection (2) or (3) shall have effect where—
-- src:2732 | (a) an award of universal credit is in force in favour of any person (“the recipient”), and
-- src:2733 | (b) an alteration—
-- src:2734 | (i) in any element of universal credit,
-- src:2735 | (ii) in the recipient's benefit income,
-- src:2736 | (iii) in any amount to be deducted in respect of earned income under section 8(3)(a) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012,
-- src:2737 | (iv) in any component of a contribution-based jobseeker's allowance,
-- src:2738 | (v) in any component of a contributory employment and support allowance, or
-- src:2739 | (vi) in such other matters as may be prescribed,
-- src:2740 | affects the computation of the amount of universal credit to which he is entitled.
-- src:2741 | (2) Where, as a result of the alteration, the amount of universal credit to which the recipient is entitled is increased or reduced, then, as from the commencing date, the amount of universal credit payable in the case of the recipient under the award shall be the increased or reduced amount, without any further decision of the Secretary of State; and the award shall have effect accordingly.
@ref sch 2 SSAA 159D(1) (src:2731-2741)
GIVEN `an award of universal credit is in force in favour of the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an alteration affects the computation of the amount of universal credit to which the recipient is entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an exception or condition regulations prescribe takes the case out of subsection (2) or (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount of universal credit to which the recipient is entitled after the alteration` IS A NUMBER
      `the commencing date` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 2 SSAA 159D(2) the amount of universal credit payable on the day without any further decision` MEANS
    IF `an award of universal credit is in force in favour of the recipient`
       AND `an alteration affects the computation of the amount of universal credit to which the recipient is entitled`
       AND day AT LEAST `the commencing date`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `an exception or condition regulations prescribe takes the case out of subsection (2) or (3)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to such exceptions and conditions as may be prescribed"; where one applies the section says nothing
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING
        -- the text's own yes: "as from the commencing date, the amount of universal credit payable ... shall be the increased or reduced amount, without any further decision"
        OTHERWISE JUST `the amount of universal credit to which the recipient is entitled after the alteration`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) applies where an award is in force and an alteration affects the computation, "as from the commencing date"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 159D(3) "Where, notwithstanding the alteration, the recipient continues on and after the commencing date to be entitled to
-- the same amount by way of universal credit as before, the award shall continue in force accordingly."
-- src:2742 | (3) Where, notwithstanding the alteration, the recipient continues on and after the commencing date to be entitled to the same amount by way of universal credit as before, the award shall continue in force accordingly.
@ref sch 2 SSAA 159D(3) (src:2742-2742)
GIVEN `an award of universal credit is in force in favour of the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient continues on and after the commencing date to be entitled to the same amount of universal credit as before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 SSAA 159D(3) the award continues in force` MEANS
    IF `an award of universal credit is in force in favour of the recipient`
       AND `the recipient continues on and after the commencing date to be entitled to the same amount of universal credit as before`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) is for the case where the recipient "continues ... to be entitled to the same amount"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 160C(2) "If, as a result of the recipient or other person reaching the qualifying age, the recipient becomes entitled to an
-- increased amount of universal credit, the amount payable ... shall, as from the day on which he becomes so entitled, be that
-- increased amount, without any further decision of the Secretary of State". (3) "Subsection (2) does not apply where ... a
-- question arises in relation to the recipient's entitlement to (a) a benefit under the Contribution and Benefits Act, or (b)
-- personal independence payment." (4) "Subsection (2) does not apply where ... a question arises in relation to the recipient's
-- entitlement to universal credit, other than (a) the question whether the element concerned, or any other element, becomes or
-- ceases to be applicable, or applicable at a particular rate ..., and (b) the question whether, in consequence, the amount of
-- his universal credit falls to be varied."
-- src:2763 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:2764 | (a) an award of universal credit is in force in favour of a person (“the recipient”), and
-- src:2765 | (b) an element has become applicable, or applicable at a particular rate, because he or some other person has reached a particular age (“the qualifying age”).
-- src:2766 | (2) If, as a result of the recipient or other person reaching the qualifying age, the recipient becomes entitled to an increased amount of universal credit, the amount payable to or for him under the award shall, as from the day on which he becomes so entitled, be that increased amount, without any further decision of the Secretary of State; and the award shall have effect accordingly.
-- src:2767 | (3) Subsection (2) does not apply where, in consequence of the recipient or other person reaching the qualifying age, a question arises in relation to the recipient's entitlement to—
-- src:2768 | (a) a benefit under the Contribution and Benefits Act, or
-- src:2769 | (b) personal independence payment.
-- src:2770 | (4) Subsection (2) does not apply where, in consequence of the recipient or other person reaching the qualifying age, a question arises in relation to the recipient's entitlement to universal credit, other than—
-- src:2771 | (a) the question whether the element concerned, or any other element, becomes or ceases to be applicable, or applicable at a particular rate, in the recipient's case, and
-- src:2772 | (b) the question whether, in consequence, the amount of his universal credit falls to be varied.
@ref sch 2 SSAA 160C(2) (src:2763-2772)
GIVEN `an award of universal credit is in force in favour of the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an element has become applicable, or applicable at a particular rate, because the recipient or some other person reached a particular age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as a result the recipient becomes entitled to an increased amount of universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a question arises as to entitlement to a benefit under the Contribution and Benefits Act or to personal independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a question arises as to entitlement to universal credit other than whether an element applies or the amount falls to be varied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 SSAA 160C(2) the increased amount is payable from the day without any further decision` MEANS
    IF `an award of universal credit is in force in favour of the recipient`
       AND `an element has become applicable, or applicable at a particular rate, because the recipient or some other person reached a particular age`
       AND `as a result the recipient becomes entitled to an increased amount of universal credit`
    THEN
        IF `a question arises as to entitlement to a benefit under the Contribution and Benefits Act or to personal independence payment`
           OR `a question arises as to entitlement to universal credit other than whether an element applies or the amount falls to be varied`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) does not apply where, in consequence of the recipient or other person reaching the qualifying age, a question arises"
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 160C "applies where" an award is in force and an element has become applicable because of a particular age
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Schedule 2 -- Social Security Act 1998, sections 8, 39 and Schedules 2 and 3`

-- 39(1) "'claimant', in relation to a couple jointly claiming universal credit, means the couple or either member of the couple".
DECLARE `sch 2 SSA1998 39(1) who is the claimant` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 SSA1998 39(1) the couple`
    `sch 2 SSA1998 39(1) either member of the couple`
    `sch 2 SSA1998 39(1) someone else`

-- src:2845 | In section 39 (interpretation), in subsection (1), before the definition of “health care professional” there is inserted—
-- src:2846 | “claimant”, in relation to a couple jointly claiming universal credit, means the couple or either member of the couple;
@ref sch 2 SSA1998 39(1) (src:2845-2846)
GIVEN who IS A `sch 2 SSA1998 39(1) who is the claimant`
      `the couple is jointly claiming universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 SSA1998 39(1) this is the claimant in relation to the couple` MEANS
    IF `the couple is jointly claiming universal credit`
    THEN
        CONSIDER who
        WHEN `sch 2 SSA1998 39(1) the couple` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 2 SSA1998 39(1) either member of the couple` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'claimant' ... means the couple or either member of the couple" (a definition)
        WHEN `sch 2 SSA1998 39(1) someone else` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the definition is "in relation to a couple jointly claiming universal credit"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Schedule 2 to the 1998 Act is headed "(decisions against which no appeal lies)" and Schedule 3 "(decisions against which an
-- appeal lies)" in the amending words; the amendments add a decision to each. Whether an appeal lies is read from the Schedule
-- the decision is added to (a lawyer's reading, listed in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `sch 2 SSA1998 decision` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 SSA1998 Sch 2 para 6(b)(v) a decision under section 159D(1)(b) of the Administration Act (universal credit)`
    `sch 2 SSA1998 Sch 2 new paragraph a decision as to the amount of benefit determined by an increase of universal credit under section 160C(2)`
    `sch 2 SSA1998 Sch 3 new paragraph a decision as to the amount of a relevant benefit payable by virtue of regulations under section 6B, 7, 8 or 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001`
    `sch 2 SSA1998 some other decision`

-- src:2847 | (1) Schedule 2 (decisions against which no appeal lies) is amended as follows.
-- src:2848 | (2) In paragraph 6(b), at the end there is inserted
-- src:2849 | or
-- src:2850 | (v) section 159D(1)(b) of that Act (universal credit).
-- src:2851 | (3) After paragraph 7 there is inserted—
-- src:2852 | Increases in universal credit due to attainment of particular ages
-- src:2853 | A decision as to the amount of benefit to which a person is entitled, where it appears to the Secretary of State that the amount is determined by the recipient's entitlement to an increased amount of universal credit in the circumstances referred to in section 160C(2) of the Administration Act.
-- src:2854 | In Schedule 3 (decisions against which an appeal lies), after paragraph 3 there is inserted—
-- src:2855 | A decision as to the amount of a relevant benefit that is payable to a person by virtue of regulations under section 6B, 7, 8 or 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001.
@ref sch 2 SSA1998 Sch 2 and Sch 3 (src:2847-2855)
GIVEN decision IS A `sch 2 SSA1998 decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 SSA1998 an appeal lies against the decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER decision
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): added to "Schedule 2 (decisions against which no appeal lies)"
    WHEN `sch 2 SSA1998 Sch 2 para 6(b)(v) a decision under section 159D(1)(b) of the Administration Act (universal credit)` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): added to "Schedule 2 (decisions against which no appeal lies)"
    WHEN `sch 2 SSA1998 Sch 2 new paragraph a decision as to the amount of benefit determined by an increase of universal credit under section 160C(2)` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- the text says yes: added to "Schedule 3 (decisions against which an appeal lies)"
    WHEN `sch 2 SSA1998 Sch 3 new paragraph a decision as to the amount of a relevant benefit payable by virtue of regulations under section 6B, 7, 8 or 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a decision the Schedule does not add to either list is not covered here
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Schedule 2 -- Social Security Fraud Act 2001, sections 6A, 6B, 7 and 9`

-- 6A(1) in the definition of "disqualifying benefit", at the beginning there is inserted "(za) any benefit under Part 1 of the
-- Welfare Reform Act 2012 (universal credit) or under any provision having effect in Northern Ireland corresponding to that Part".
-- Seam 7 of PLAN.md section 8: wra4's sections 117 to 119 add the other limbs; this function is wra1's limb only.
-- src:2867 | In section 6A (definitions), in subsection (1), in the definition of “disqualifying benefit”, at the beginning there is inserted—
-- src:2868 | (za) any benefit under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (universal credit) or under any provision having effect in Northern Ireland corresponding to that Part;
@ref sch 2 SSFA 6A(1)(za) (src:2867-2868)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 SSFA 6A(1)(za) the benefit is a disqualifying benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `universal credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed here): this limb names universal credit only; the other limbs of the definition are in the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 and in wra4's range (ss 117 to 119)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- 6B(5A) "The Secretary of State may by regulations provide that, where the sanctionable benefit is universal credit, the
-- benefit shall be payable, during the whole or a part of any period comprised in the disqualification period, as if one or more
-- of the following applied (a) the amount payable were reduced in such manner as may be prescribed; (b) the benefit were payable
-- only if there is compliance by the offender with such obligations with respect to the provision of information as may be
-- imposed by the regulations; (c) the benefit were payable only if the circumstances are otherwise such as may be prescribed;
-- (d) any amount of the benefit payable in prescribed circumstances were recoverable by the Secretary of State."
DECLARE `sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A) way universal credit may be made payable` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A)(a) the amount payable reduced in the manner prescribed`
    `sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A)(b) payable only if the offender complies with information obligations the regulations impose`
    `sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A)(c) payable only if the circumstances are otherwise as prescribed`
    `sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A)(d) any amount payable in prescribed circumstances recoverable by the Secretary of State`
    `sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A) some other way`

-- src:2872 | (5A) The Secretary of State may by regulations provide that, where the sanctionable benefit is universal credit, the benefit shall be payable, during the whole or a part of any period comprised in the disqualification period, as if one or more of the following applied—
-- src:2873 | (a) the amount payable were reduced in such manner as may be prescribed;
-- src:2874 | (b) the benefit were payable only if there is compliance by the offender with such obligations with respect to the provision of information as may be imposed by the regulations;
-- src:2875 | (c) the benefit were payable only if the circumstances are otherwise such as may be prescribed;
-- src:2876 | (d) any amount of the benefit payable in prescribed circumstances were recoverable by the Secretary of State.
@ref sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A) (src:2872-2876)
GIVEN way IS A `sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A) way universal credit may be made payable`
      `the sanctionable benefit is universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A) regulations may provide that universal credit is payable as if this applied` MEANS
    IF `the sanctionable benefit is universal credit`
    THEN
        CONSIDER way
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A)(a) the amount payable reduced in the manner prescribed` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A)(b) payable only if the offender complies with information obligations the regulations impose` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A)(c) payable only if the circumstances are otherwise as prescribed` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A)(d) any amount payable in prescribed circumstances recoverable by the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for "one or more of the following"
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 6B(5A) some other way` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "where the sanctionable benefit is universal credit"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 7(2A) the same four ways, for a second or subsequent conviction.
DECLARE `sch 2 SSFA 7(2A) way universal credit may be made payable` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 SSFA 7(2A)(a) the amount payable reduced in the manner prescribed`
    `sch 2 SSFA 7(2A)(b) payable only if the offender complies with information obligations the regulations impose`
    `sch 2 SSFA 7(2A)(c) payable only if the circumstances are otherwise as prescribed`
    `sch 2 SSFA 7(2A)(d) any amount payable in prescribed circumstances recoverable by the Secretary of State`
    `sch 2 SSFA 7(2A) some other way`

-- src:2882 | (2A) The Secretary of State may by regulations provide that, where the sanctionable benefit is universal credit, the benefit shall be payable, during the whole or a part of any period comprised in the disqualification period, as if one or more of the following applied—
-- src:2883 | (a) the amount payable were reduced in such manner as may be prescribed;
-- src:2884 | (b) the benefit were payable only if there is compliance by the offender with such obligations with respect to the provision of information as may be imposed by the regulations;
-- src:2885 | (c) the benefit were payable only if the circumstances are otherwise such as may be prescribed;
-- src:2886 | (d) any amount of the benefit payable in prescribed circumstances were recoverable by the Secretary of State.
@ref sch 2 SSFA 7(2A) (src:2882-2886)
GIVEN way IS A `sch 2 SSFA 7(2A) way universal credit may be made payable`
      `the sanctionable benefit is universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 SSFA 7(2A) regulations may provide that universal credit is payable as if this applied` MEANS
    IF `the sanctionable benefit is universal credit`
    THEN
        CONSIDER way
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 7(2A)(a) the amount payable reduced in the manner prescribed` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 7(2A)(b) payable only if the offender complies with information obligations the regulations impose` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 7(2A)(c) payable only if the circumstances are otherwise as prescribed` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 7(2A)(d) any amount payable in prescribed circumstances recoverable by the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for "one or more of the following"
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 7(2A) some other way` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "where the sanctionable benefit is universal credit"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 9(2A) "In relation to cases in which the benefit is universal credit, the provision that may be made by virtue of subsection
-- (2) is provision that, in the case of the offender's family member, any universal credit shall be payable ... as if one or
-- more of the following applied": the same four ways, with (b) extended to the offender's family member.
DECLARE `sch 2 SSFA 9(2A) way universal credit may be made payable` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 SSFA 9(2A)(a) the amount payable reduced in the manner prescribed`
    `sch 2 SSFA 9(2A)(b) payable only if the offender or the offender's family member, or both, comply with information obligations the regulations impose`
    `sch 2 SSFA 9(2A)(c) payable only if the circumstances are otherwise as prescribed`
    `sch 2 SSFA 9(2A)(d) any amount payable in prescribed circumstances recoverable by the Secretary of State`
    `sch 2 SSFA 9(2A) some other way`

-- src:2902 | (2A) In relation to cases in which the benefit is universal credit, the provision that may be made by virtue of subsection (2) is provision that, in the case of the offender's family member, any universal credit shall be payable, during the whole or a part of any period comprised in the relevant period, as if one or more of the following applied—
-- src:2903 | (a) the amount payable were reduced in such manner as may be prescribed;
-- src:2904 | (b) the benefit were payable only if there is compliance by the offender or the offender's family member, or both of them, with such obligations with respect to the provision of information as may be imposed by the regulations;
-- src:2905 | (c) the benefit were payable only if the circumstances are otherwise such as may be prescribed;
-- src:2906 | (d) any amount of the benefit payable in prescribed circumstances were recoverable by the Secretary of State.
@ref sch 2 SSFA 9(2A) (src:2902-2906)
GIVEN way IS A `sch 2 SSFA 9(2A) way universal credit may be made payable`
      `the benefit is universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 SSFA 9(2A) regulations may provide that the family member's universal credit is payable as if this applied` MEANS
    IF `the benefit is universal credit`
    THEN
        CONSIDER way
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 9(2A)(a) the amount payable reduced in the manner prescribed` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 9(2A)(b) payable only if the offender or the offender's family member, or both, comply with information obligations the regulations impose` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 9(2A)(c) payable only if the circumstances are otherwise as prescribed` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 9(2A)(d) any amount payable in prescribed circumstances recoverable by the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision is "one or more of the following"
        WHEN `sch 2 SSFA 9(2A) some other way` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision is "in relation to cases in which the benefit is universal credit"
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Schedule 2 -- State Pension Credit Act 2002, section 4`

-- (1A) "A claimant is not entitled to state pension credit if he is a member of a couple the other member of which has not
-- attained the qualifying age."
-- src:2918 | In section 4 of the State Pension Credit Act 2002 (exclusions), after subsection (1) there is inserted—
-- src:2919 | (1A) A claimant is not entitled to state pension credit if he is a member of a couple the other member of which has not attained the qualifying age.
@ref sch 2 SPCA 4(1A) (src:2918-2919)
GIVEN `the claimant is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other member of the couple has attained the qualifying age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 SPCA 4(1A) the claimant is entitled to state pension credit` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is a member of a couple` AND (NOT `the other member of the couple has attained the qualifying age`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant is not entitled to state pension credit if he is a member of a couple the other member of which has not attained the qualifying age"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1A) bars entitlement in that case; it does not give entitlement in any other
    ELSE NOTHING
